<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edmund Hillary</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1919–2008</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sir Edmund Hillary</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edmund Hillary was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> mountaineer and explorer who, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenzing-norgay">Sherpa Tenzing</a> Norgay, made the first confirmed ascent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-everest">Mount Everest</a> on 29 May 1953. He later reached the South Pole overland in 1958 during the Commonwealth Trans-Antarctic Expedition. Through the Himalayan Trust he built schools and hospitals for the Sherpa people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, and he appears on New Zealand's five-dollar note.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edmund-hillary.jpg" alt="Edmund Hillary" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photographer unidentified. Retouched by TimofKingsland. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edmund_Hillary,_c._1953,_autograph_removed.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
